{"term":"ozone","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:7c004fc335babdb942","definition":"An allotrope of oxygen (symbol O₃) having three atoms in the molecule instead of the usual two; it is a toxic gas, generated from oxygen by electrical discharge.","example":"Lightning flashed again, the thunder came a second later. It rained harder. The smell of ozone was strong. You could feel the charge in the air.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"usually","register":"uncountable, usually","wordFamily":["acetozone","antiozonant","antiozone","anti-ozone","antozone","bozone","iodozone","nonozone","ozonate","ozonation","ozonator","ozone bath","ozone-friendly","ozone hole","ozone layer","ozonelike","ozone-like","ozone paper","ozone resistance","ozone shield","ozone sickness","ozonesonde","ozone therapy","ozoney","ozonic","ozonide","ozoniferous","ozonification","ozonify","ozonisation"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ozone#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:6ac205730368b61154","definition":"Fresh air, especially that breathed at the seaside and smelling of seaweed.","example":"A patent obtained in England, and specified far from clearly, for obtaining ozone by boiling seaweed,†† may be mentioned as a curiosity, and also the credulity with which ozone-baths, prepared in this manner, find a ready sale, in spite of, or perhaps rather on account of, their high price.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"UK, informal, usually","register":"UK, informal, uncountable, usually","wordFamily":["acetozone","antiozonant","antiozone","anti-ozone","antozone","bozone","iodozone","nonozone","ozonate","ozonation","ozonator","ozone bath","ozone-friendly","ozone hole","ozone layer","ozonelike","ozone-like","ozone paper","ozone resistance","ozone shield","ozone sickness","ozonesonde","ozone therapy","ozoney","ozonic","ozonide","ozoni